# Commit unsigned at end of turn

For **this repository** (Entmoot):

1. **When:** At the end of a turn, if there are durable intentional changes worth
   keeping (code, contracts, tests, docs that belong in git), create a commit.
   Do not leave finished work uncommitted waiting for an explicit “please commit.”
2. **How:** Use `git commit --no-gpg-sign` (or
   `git -c commit.gpgsign=false commit …`). Global `commit.gpgsign=true` must not
   block agent commits here. Do **not** change git config; do **not** use
   `--no-verify`.
3. **Hygiene:** Follow the usual commit protocol (status/diff/log, focused
   message, stage only relevant files, no secrets, no force push, no amend unless
   the amend rules already allow it).
4. **Skip:** Do not commit scratch under `.tmp/`, secrets, or unrelated dirty
   worktree noise. If nothing durable changed, do not create an empty commit.

This project rule overrides the general “only commit when asked” preference for
this repo only.
